# The ninth tooling step's breaks.

# The core rig (item 3).

[break] rig-a-wait-for-a-question-never-gives-up
rule: The core rig's wait for a question fails at once when the session goes idle with nothing asked.
file: crates/cortex-core/tests/it/main.rs
in: Front::approval
find: open(seen).is_some() || idles_in(seen) > idle_before
replace: open(seen).is_some()
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::a_wait_for_a_question_the_turn_never_asks_fails_at_once

[break] rig-a-wait-for-a-question-gives-up-at-a-turns-end
rule: The core rig's wait for a question goes on while a turn is queued behind the one that ended.
file: crates/cortex-core/tests/it/main.rs
in: Front::approval
find: open(seen).is_some() || idles_in(seen) > idle_before
replace: open(seen).is_some() || ends_in(seen).len() > idle_before
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::a_wait_for_a_question_goes_on_while_a_turn_is_queued

[break] rig-a-turns-end-is-taken-for-idle
rule: The session is idle when it says so, not when a turn ends.
file: crates/cortex-core/tests/it/main.rs
in: idles_in
find: event: Event::SessionIdle(_)
replace: event: Event::TurnCompleted(_)
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::a_wait_for_a_question_goes_on_while_a_turn_is_queued

[break] rig-told-takes-any-notice
rule: `told` waits for a notice that says what it was given.
file: crates/cortex-core/tests/it/main.rs
in: Front::told
find: .find(|(index, notice)| !taken.contains(index) && notice.contains(text))
replace: .find(|(index, _)| !taken.contains(index))
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::a_notice_is_waited_for_and_a_refused_turn_names_what_asked

[break] rig-turn-denying-allows
rule: `turn_denying` refuses every call that is asked about.
file: crates/cortex-core/tests/it/main.rs
in: Front::turn_denying
find: self.turn_answering(text, |_| ApprovalChoice::Deny).await
replace: self.turn_answering(text, |_| ApprovalChoice::AllowOnce).await
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::a_notice_is_waited_for_and_a_refused_turn_names_what_asked

